  "summary": {
    "observable": "G0W0 sampled path gap",
    "value": 1.6394,
    "unit": "eV",
    "gw_gap_ev": 1.6394,
    "gap_definition": "G0W0@PBE gap on the Gamma-X-M-Gamma-R-X sampled path (61 points, 12 per segment, exclusive endpoint convention). Raw CBM(empty) minus VBM(occupied) over all 832 declared bands. Not a global Brillouin-zone gap and not a convergence claim.",
    "scope": "Si 64-atom simple-cubic supercell (a = 20.4718 Bohr, 2x2x2 of the 8-atom cell), ONCV PBE PP with 2s2p1d NAO (13 functions per atom) and a preset 6s5p6d4f4g1h1i auxiliary basis (139 functions per atom, 8896 total). SCF on a 3x3x3 Gamma-centered mesh with symmetry on (4 IBZ q-points), NSCF on the 61-point Line path with symmetry off, G0W0 with option_dielect_func=53 (full head+wing plus the Gamma s-head correction), replace_w_head on, use_scalapack_gw_wc on, nfreq 16.",
    "notes": "The auxiliary basis is a preset .abfs read through STRU ABFS_ORBITAL with exx_pca_threshold 10, so the PCA-constructed remainder contributes essentially nothing. It was generated from a for_aux 2s2p1d1f orbital at exx_pca_threshold 1e-4; the extra f channel is auxiliary-only and is not part of the physical NAO. The same SCF with the same physical NAO but a 60-function auxiliary basis gives 1.5413 eV on this path, so the auxiliary-basis effect here is +0.098 eV. A head-only dielectric (option_dielect_func=4) gives 2.4362 eV and is not a valid GW observable."
  },
